 "response": "Kribun's budget is now $3,216K.\n\n**How I got there**\n\n- **Which records count:** Only Finance Office updates change the budget. All PMO, Vendor, Sales, Engineering, Marketing, Facilities, Operations and Legal messages are ignored. Non-budget Finance items, such as audit notes, reminders and purchase orders, are also ignored.\n- **Withdrawal chains:** Withdrawals can target other withdrawals, so I traced each chain back from its last, untargeted link. Withdrawal steps then alternate in effect. Three examples:\n  - Update #0003 (\u2212$247K) still applies. Its chain runs back from #1291, which leaves the withdrawal of #0003 by #0006 cancelled.\n  - #0105 (\u2212$516K) still applies. Its chain runs back from #1037, and #0109's withdrawal of #0105 ends up cancelled.\n  - #0912 (+$596K) still applies, because #1578 cancels #1478's withdrawal of it.\n  - Several others are finally withdrawn, including #0026, #0032, #0069, #0106, #0133, #0318, #0946 and #1268 (withdrawn by #1561).\n- **Calculation:** I started from the $2,520K set in #0001. I then applied every Finance Office increase and decrease that remains in effect, once each and in order. The last effective update is #1597 (\u2212$60K), which takes the running total from $3,276K to $3,216K.\n\nThis is a single running total across roughly 600 updates, done by hand. I did not perform an independent second pass.\n\nANSWER: $3216K",
